{"data": [{"author_id": "2099830333856235520", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:14:15.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117425087385383146"], "id": "2117425087385383146", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2110603562288062464", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117373827621814464", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@thataibloke @OpenAI Agree, quotes and invoice totals are where one wrong number costs real money. Whatever tool does the admin, having the math computed in code and a person check the finished file is the part we'd want proven first.", "url": "https://x.com/Gryndara/status/2117425087385383146"}, {"author_id": "1934516722025017344", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:10:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117424056127660047"], "id": "2117424056127660047", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1974240295371100160", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117311536817434915", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@yv_thorne @OpenAI 개방적 같은 소리하고 있네", "url": "https://x.com/beluga_alpha/status/2117424056127660047"}, {"author_id": "1332999084253138945", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:06:38.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117423169464356901"], "id": "2117423169464356901", "in_reply_to_user_id": "4398626122", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117307611338997846", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@OpenAI LifeVal is the right bet — most users want help with school runs and bills, not AGI mythology. Watching Doubao and Quark compete in China, the everyday-assistant race will be won by local integrations and trust, not just the biggest model card.", "url": "https://x.com/matrixaifund/status/2117423169464356901"}, {"author_id": "1656168114978017281", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:00:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117421697577914596"], "id": "2117421697577914596", "in_reply_to_user_id": "4398626122", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117307611338997846", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@OpenAI Finding childcare is the real Turing test. Nice to see a benchmark built from actual users.", "url": "https://x.com/ucdops/status/2117421697577914596"}, {"author_id": "1922921330699120640", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:00:07.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117421531923984392"], "id": "2117421531923984392", "in_reply_to_user_id": "4398626122", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117307611338997846", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@OpenAI LifeVal 有意思的地方不在任务清单，而在评分尺子。找托育、办政务、管钱这三类事，答案很少只有一个标准解，上下文一变就变。过去一年用它来量化和改进模型，真正难的是把“办成了”拆成可复核的步骤，不然榜单分涨了，日常用起来还是差口气。 #LifeVal", "url": "https://x.com/DJC125765252591/status/2117421531923984392"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["16_2117421204504190976"]}, "author_id": "1152907620186877955", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:58:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117421213459038236"], "id": "2117421213459038236", "in_reply_to_user_id": "4398626122", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117307611338997846", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@OpenAI Do we need to kneel to them? @elonmusk @realDonaldTrump https://t.co/aZxLatSNqS", "url": "https://x.com/hwantion1/status/2117421213459038236"}, {"author_id": "1487212454870458374", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:54:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117420082460864846"], "id": "2117420082460864846", "in_reply